  "description": "YINKAL crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 4/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C112 H100 Cl1 Dy9 N24 O44 1+,4(C1 H4 O1),Cl1 1-. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2B (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3B (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2C (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3C (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4? (Dy) has 0 O neighbors; Dy5? (Dy) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.522-4.230 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.15-127.93°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy9(L)8(CH3O)4(μ4-Cl)(CH3OH)4(H2O)4]Cl·3CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
